paired    (optimistic) mean difference -0.0017  sd 0.0020  95% CI [-0.0022, -0.0011]  t = -5.76  p = 0.0000  wins 10/50
corrected (quote this) 95% CI [-0.0038, +0.0005]  t = -1.57  p = 0.1236

The corrected row is Nadeau & Bengio: it inflates the variance to admit
that each fold's model trains on the other 4, so the observations are not
independent. Its p-value is always the larger of the two, and it is the one to
quote - a difference that only clears 0.05 uncorrected has not cleared it.

best_shorter is -0.0017 worse than quantiles_flank_depth_augmented, winning 10/50 paired observations. The uncorrected paired test says p = 0.0000; corrected for the overlap between training sets it is p = 0.1236, which does not clear 0.05. Read the win count: a difference that holds on every paired observation is worth more than this p-value suggests, and more repetitions (--repeats 10) are the way to settle it rather than quoting the uncorrected number.

